#: R/decision.b.R
msgid ""
"95% intervals for sensitivity, specificity, predictive values at the sample "
"prevalence, likelihood ratios, diagnostic odds ratio and Youden's index "
"(tick 95% confidence intervals)"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"A = 1 - within-case variance / total variance (Robinson 1957): 1 means every "
"rater gave every case the same value. Raters who agree no better than chance "
"score about 1/%6$d here, not 0, so the label is read from the "
"chance-corrected value (%6$d A - 1) / %7$d = %8$.3f, which is 0 at chance. "
"%1$s (A = %2$.3f). The interval is a percentile bootstrap over cases (%3$d "
"resamples, seed %4$d) at the %5$d%% level. Bands used for the label, on the "
"chance-corrected value: below 0.50 poor, 0.50 to 0.75 moderate, 0.75 to 0.90 "
"good, 0.90 and above excellent."
msgstr ""

#: R/decision.b.R
msgid ""
"A blank likelihood ratio is not estimable from these counts: its denominator "
"count is zero, so it would be infinite, and the continuity correction (0.5 "
"added to every cell) would not keep it above 1. Read the sensitivity and "
"specificity with their confidence intervals instead."
msgstr ""

#: R/decision.b.R
msgid ""
"A blank ratio is not estimable from these counts: its denominator count is "
"zero, so it would be infinite, and the continuity correction (0.5 added to "
"every cell) would not keep it above 1."
msgstr ""

#: R/kappaSizeFixedN.b.R
msgid ""
"A bound at or below zero means this many subjects cannot rule out agreement "
"no better than chance."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"A case ID variable was given, but no case appears under more than one "
"condition, so this is still a comparison between cases."
msgstr ""

#: R/decision.b.R
msgid ""
"A cell of the 2x2 table is zero. A likelihood ratio whose denominator count "
"is zero would be infinite, so it is computed from the Haldane-Anscombe "
"corrected table (0.5 added to every cell) and reflects that correction, not "
"the observed data: the positive likelihood ratio when specificity is 100%, "
"the negative likelihood ratio when specificity is 0%. Sensitivity, "
"specificity, accuracy, the predictive values and any other likelihood ratio "
"use the observed counts."
msgstr ""

#: R/decision.b.R
msgid ""
"A cell of the 2x2 table is zero. A ratio whose denominator count is zero "
"would be infinite (LR+: no false positives; LR-: no true negatives; "
"diagnostic odds ratio: no false positives or no false negatives), so it is "
"computed from the Haldane-Anscombe corrected table (0.5 added to every "
"cell). A ratio whose numerator count is zero is exactly 0 and is not "
"corrected. Sensitivity, specificity, accuracy, the predictive values and "
"every other ratio use the observed counts, so a corrected, finite likelihood "
"ratio can sit beside a sensitivity or specificity of 0% or 100%."
msgstr ""

#: R/decision.b.R
msgid ""
"A cell of the 2x2 table is zero. A ratio whose denominator count is zero "
"would be infinite, so it is computed from the Haldane-Anscombe corrected "
"table (0.5 added to every cell). The other rows use the observed counts."
msgstr ""

#: R/decision.b.R
msgid ""
"A cell of the 2x2 table is zero. A ratio whose denominator count is zero "
"would be infinite, so it is computed from the Haldane-Anscombe corrected "
"table (0.5 added to every cell). The other rows use the observed counts. "
"Because the ratios do not all come from the same table, the diagnostic odds "
"ratio shown need not equal LR+ / LR- as displayed."
msgstr ""

#: R/decision.b.R
msgid ""
"A cell of the 2x2 table was zero. A likelihood ratio whose denominator count "
"is zero would be infinite, so it is computed from the Haldane-Anscombe "
"corrected table (0.5 added to every cell); a likelihood ratio with a zero "
"numerator count is exactly 0 and is not corrected. Sensitivity, specificity "
"and the predictive values above are not corrected."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"A cluster with one member has no within-cluster similarity, so that row is "
"left blank."
msgstr ""

#: package.description
msgid ""
"A comprehensive toolkit for medical decision analysis and reliability\n"
"assessment, implemented as a jamovi module. The package provides tools for:\n"
"* Interrater and intrarater reliability analysis using Cohen's Kappa and\n"
"  Fleiss' Kappa statistics\n"
"* Diagnostic test evaluation with sensitivity, specificity, predictive "
"values,\n"
"  and likelihood ratios\n"
"* Sample size calculations for reliability studies using confidence interval\n"
"  and power-based approaches\n"
"* Visualization tools including Fagan nomograms for Bayesian probability\n"
"  updates\n"
"* Power analysis for interobserver agreement studies with support for\n"
"  multiple raters and outcome categories\n"
"Tools are provided through an intuitive graphical interface in jamovi, "
"making\n"
"complex medical decision analyses accessible to clinical researchers.\n"
"For comments, suggestions, feature requests or reporting bugs, please open "
"an issue at <https://github.com/sbalci/ClinicoPathJamoviModule/issues/>."
msgstr ""

#: R/enhancedROC.b.R
msgid ""
"A flexible calibration curve gives ICI, E50, E90 and Emax as defined by "
"Austin & Steyerberg (2019); it is fitted here as a natural cubic spline of "
"the logit of the predicted risk with %s knots, a variant of their loess and "
"restricted cubic spline curves on the probability scale."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncurve.b.R
msgid ""
"A gain at or below zero means a default strategy serves these patients at "
"least as well as the model."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncombine.b.R
msgid "A gold standard variable is required. Select a reference test."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"A headline kappa says how well the panel agrees as a whole. This section "
"asks the questions a pathology department asks next: how the study was read, "
"whether any pathologist grades systematically higher or lower than "
"colleagues, at which grade boundary the difference lies, and how much of the "
"variation between readings comes from the cases rather than from the "
"pathologists."
msgstr ""

#: R/enhancedROC.b.R
msgid "A higher prevalence raises the positive predictive value."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"A kappa below 0.40 means the raters agreed little more often than chance "
"alone would produce, so in these data one rater's category does not reliably "
"predict another's. Before reading that as a rater problem, look at the Data "
"Summary: when nearly all cases fall into one category, kappa can be low even "
"though the raters matched on most cases - compare it with the Agreement % "
"above."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"A kappa between 0.40 and 0.60 means the raters agreed moderately more often "
"than chance alone would produce. It is not the proportion of cases they "
"matched on - that is the Agreement % above, which with three or more raters "
"counts only the cases they ALL matched on. A rare rating category can also "
"hold kappa down while raw matching stays high; any low-prevalence note under "
"the table flags that."
msgstr ""

#: R/nogoldstandard.b.R
msgid "A latent-class EM point estimator using fixed Beta priors."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncalculator.b.R
msgid ""
"A likelihood ratio is not estimable for this table (see the notices above), "
"so it cannot be placed on the nomogram."
msgstr ""

#: R/decision.b.R
msgid ""
"A likelihood ratio of exactly 0 is the observed value: its numerator count "
"is zero (no true positives for LR+, no false negatives for LR-), so no "
"correction is applied."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncalculator.b.R
msgid ""
"A likelihood ratio whose denominator cell is empty uses the Haldane-Anscombe "
"0.5 correction, and so do the probabilities read from the nomogram. The "
"predictive values and post-test probabilities in the Measures table are "
"computed from the raw counts and can differ, by a wide margin in a small "
"table."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncalculator.b.R
msgid ""
"A likelihood ratio whose denominator cell is empty uses the Haldane-Anscombe "
"0.5 correction, while the predictive values above use the observed counts. "
"Multiplying the pre-test odds by these likelihood ratios therefore need not "
"reproduce the predictive values exactly."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"A linear mixed-effects model that compares measurement conditions (e.g., "
"AI-assisted vs.\n"
"                    conventional scoring) while properly accounting for the "
"crossed structure of rater x case data."
msgstr ""

