#: R/decisioncombine.b.R
msgid ""
"Corrected J estimates how a rule picked by this ranking would score in new "
"patients like these. The whole ranking was repeated in {nboot} bootstrap "
"samples drawn within each reference group; Expected drop is the average "
"amount by which the rule picked in a sample scored higher there than in the "
"original data (Monte Carlo standard error {mcse}). The highest-ranked rule "
"was picked again in {stability}% of the samples. The correction is "
"approximate: it leaves part of the optimism when rules are nearly tied, and "
"it does not allow for how the tests, levels or patients were chosen."
msgstr ""

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"Corrected values are an optimism-corrected internal validation (Harrell's "
"bootstrap) on the same patients, not an external validation. With variable "
"and lambda selection in a modest sample the correction removes only part of "
"the optimism, so the corrected AUC can still be too high; confirm "
"performance on independent data."
msgstr ""

