#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"Correlation distance compares a case's rating profile across raters, and "
"with two raters that profile has two points, so the correlation between any "
"two cases is exactly +1 or -1 and the metric cannot separate them. Choose "
"the Euclidean or Manhattan metric, or add a third rater."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"Correlation distance compares the shape of a case's ratings across raters, "
"not their level, so cases rated alike in pattern are grouped together "
"however far apart their values are. The widest gap between two case averages "
"inside one cluster here is {diff} units, which is {sds} times the pooled "
"standard deviation of all ratings. The Euclidean metric, which is the "
"default, and the Manhattan metric group cases by absolute value."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"Correlation distance removes systematic offsets, so raters who rank the "
"cases the same way are grouped together however far apart their readings "
"are. Here {high} and {low} share a cluster although {high} reads on average "
"{diff} units higher than {low}, which is {sds} times the pooled standard "
"deviation of all ratings. The Concordance (1 - Lin's CCC) metric, which is "
"the default, groups raters only when their readings are interchangeable."
msgstr ""

