"Each row must be a different patient: several slides, cores or lesions from "
"one patient make the confidence intervals too narrow."
msgstr ""

#: R/decision.b.R
msgid ""
"Each row must be a different, independent patient. If patients contribute "
"several specimens (cores, blocks, lesions), the confidence intervals are too "
"narrow: analyze one specimen per patient or use a method for clustered data."
msgstr ""

#: R/psychopdaROC.b.R
msgid ""
"Each row must be an independent observation. Repeated measurements from the "
"same patient require a method that accounts for clustering."
msgstr ""

#: R/psychopdaROC.b.R
msgid ""
"Each row must represent an independent observation. These confidence "
"intervals, tests and bootstrap resamples do not account for clustering or "
"repeated measurements. Multiple lesions, blocks, slides or visits from the "
"same patient require a prespecified patient-level summary or a method that "
"accounts for clustering; do not treat them as independent patients."
