"test whether agreement differs between subgroups, and nothing here is "
"adjusted for the number of subgroups compared. A subgroup's statistic also "
"depends on that subgroup's case mix: kappa falls when one rating category "
"dominates, and ICC falls when the cases within a subgroup are alike, so two "
"subgroups whose raters behave identically can still differ for that reason "
"alone."
