#: R/decisioncalculator.b.R
msgid "Youden's index below 0"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncalculator.b.R
msgid ""
"Youden's index equals sensitivity plus specificity minus one. It weights "
"sensitivity and specificity equally and is descriptive, not a clinical "
"decision threshold."
msgstr ""

#: R/decision.b.R
msgid ""
"Youden's index interval: Agresti-Caffo interval for the difference between "
"the true-positive and false-positive rates (one positive and one negative "
"result added to each group). Number needed to diagnose = 1 / Youden's index; "
"its interval is the inverse of the positive part of the Youden interval."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncalculator.b.R
msgid ""
"Youden's index intervals are not computed for scenarios containing "
"fractional frequencies because no effective sample size or weighting design "
"was supplied."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncalculator.b.R
msgid ""
"Youden's index is {youden} (95% CI {lower} to {upper}; {npos} "
"reference-positive and {nneg} reference-negative observations), and the "
"whole interval is below 0: a positive result is less common among "
"reference-positive than among reference-negative subjects. Check whether TP "
"and FN, or FP and TN, were entered in swapped positions."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncalculator.b.R
msgid ""
"Youden's index is {youden} (95% CI {lower} to {upper}), below 0 but within "
"sampling variation of 0, so this table does not show that the test "
"discriminates better than chance. If the counts are not coded as intended, "
"check whether TP and FN, or FP and TN, were swapped."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncalculator.b.R
msgid ""
"Youden's index is {youden} and sample accuracy is {accuracy}. These values "
"describe the entered study table; they are not clinical grades or decision "
"thresholds."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncalculator.b.R
msgid ""
"Youden's index is {youden}, below 0. No interval is computed for fractional "
"counts, so whether this differs from chance is not assessed. If the counts "
"are not coded as intended, check whether TP and FN, or FP and TN, were "
"swapped."
msgstr ""

#: R/decision.b.R
#: R/decisioncalculator.b.R
msgid ""
"Youden's index is 0 or below in this sample, so the number needed to "
"diagnose has no point estimate. Its confidence interval starts at the lower "
"limit shown and has no upper bound."
msgstr ""

#: R/decision.b.R
msgid ""
"Youden's index is the difference between the true positive rate and the "
"false positive rate. Youden's index ranges from -1 to +1 with values closer "
"to 1 if both sensitivity and specificity are high (i.e. close to 1)."
msgstr ""

